                "Related research for the analysis of the Quarterly Business Report - Q4 2025 includes:\n\n1. The Q4 2025 U.S. Retail Scorecard by Lipper Alpha Insight, which provides blended revenue growth estimates and earnings performance for 190 retail companies, highlighting revenue growth and earnings surprises in Q4 2025[1].\n\n2. NEPC’s Quarterly Private Markets Report for Q4 2025, offering expert analysis on market drivers, sector trends, and investment insights relevant to private markets and commercial real estate[2].\n\n3. The U.S. Bureau of Economic Analysis (BEA) advance estimate for Q4 2025 GDP, which details economic growth, R&D investment increases, and price index changes impacting the broader economy[3].\n\n4. Fidelity’s Quarterly Business Cycle Update for Q4 2025, discussing business cycle expansion amid a softer labor market and providing portfolio insights based on extensive portfolio reviews[4][15].\n\n5. Market reviews and outlooks from sources like Waverly Advisors and Cape Cod 5, which analyze fixed income, equity market performance, interest rates, and sector returns in Q4 2025[5][6].\n\n6. Corporate earnings reports such as Target Corporation’s Q4 2025 earnings, which provide detailed financial results and operational highlights for major companies[7].\n\n7. Zoomd’s Q4 and full-year 2025 financial results, illustrating revenue growth, profitability, and liquidity management in a technology-focused company[13].\n\n8. The FDIC’s Quarterly Banking Profile for Q4 2025, offering data on banking sector performance, return on assets, and net income trends[8].\n\nThese sources collectively provide comprehensive financial, operational, and economic context relevant to analyzing a Q4 2025 business report with strong revenue growth, margin expansion, R&D investment, and market expansion initiatives[1][2][3][4][5][6][7][8][13].",
