                  snippet:
                    "The blended revenue growth estimate for the 190 companies in this index is 5.1% for Q4 2025. Of those companies that have reported their quarterly results so far, 66% announced revenue that exceeded analysts’ expectations and the remaining ...\nTo date, 155 of the 190 companies in our Retail/Restaurant Index have reported their EPS results for Q4 2025, representing 82% of the index. Of those companies that have reported their quarterly results, 60% announced profits that beat analysts’ expectations, while 6% delivered on-target results and 34% reported earnings that fell below estimates.\nA widely quoted authority on the U.S. consumer and retail information, including same store sales and corporate earnings, Martis’s research has been featured in The Wall Street Journal, The New York Times, CNN Money, and Barron’s, and she has appeared on CNBC’s Power Lunch and The Nightly Business Report, as well as other financial news outlets. Q4 2025 U.S.\nThe blended revenue growth estimate for the 190 companies in this index is 5.1% for Q4 2025. Of those companies that have reported their quarterly results so far, 66% announced revenue that exceeded analysts’ expectations and the remaining 34% reported that their revenue fell below analysts’ forecasts.\nArticle Keywords earnings, Earnings Dashboard, I/B/E/S, inflation, macy's, Q4 2025, retail earnings, retail revenue, Ross Stores, Same Store Sales, SSS, Target, tariffs, Walmart ... To date, 159 of the 190 companies in our Retail/Restaurant Index have reported their EPS ...",
