                  snippet:
                    "The importance of employee training and development in strengthening engagement and upskilling, while a strong organizational culture establishes trust, inclusivity, and effective hybrid arrangements. Including these elements contributes to both increased productivity and employee job satisfaction in the evolving work environment (Zahari et al. 2024; Zhou 2025).\nThis study undertakes a systematic literature review of the impact of remote and hybrid work models on the productivity of small and medium-sized enterprises in the post-COVID-19 environment. Using the Preferred Reporting Items for Systematic Reviews and Meta-Analyses procedure, data were collected from Scopus and Web of Science, resulting in a final sample of 12 peer-reviewed studies published between 2020 and 2024 that were studied across diverse global contexts.\nSN Business & Economics - This study undertakes a systematic literature review of the impact of remote and hybrid work models on the productivity of small and medium-sized enterprises in the...\nThe importance of employee training and development in strengthening engagement and upskilling, while a strong organizational culture establishes trust, inclusivity, and effective hybrid arrangements. Including these elements contributes to both increased productivity and employee job satisfaction in the evolving work environment (Zahari et al. 2024; Zhou 2025).\nFlexible Work Schedules have been particularly beneficial in the Ghanaian SME sector, contributing to greater profitability, productivity, and employee well-being (Kokot Tomaž 2023; Ramasamy Velar and Kee 2025). FWA enabled employees to align their tasks with periods of peak productivity, resulting in enhanced job satisfaction and firm performance.",
