            digest: "Gakg8",
            data: {
              text: "## Summary of Q4 2025 Search Findings\n\n### What is Q4 2025?\nQ4 2025 refers to the **fourth fiscal quarter of 2025** (October–December), used by companies for financial reporting, earnings tracking, and business analysis.\n\n---\n\n### Key Economic & Market Highlights\n\n**Banking & Finance**\n- FDIC-insured institutions reported **$77.7 billion in net income** (ROA of 1.24%), a slight 2% decrease from Q3\n- Full-year 2025 bank net income reached **$295.6 billion**, up 10.2% from 2024\n- U.S. direct lending volumes hit **$380 billion** for the full year\n\n**Small Business**\n- The Small Business Index scored **68.4**, down from an all-time high of 72.0 in Q3\n- **Inflation** remained the top challenge; employee retention concerns also rose\n- 43% of small businesses viewed their local economy as healthy\n\n**Consumer Spending**\n- Consumers shifted toward **essentials and discount/private-label products**\n- Consumer M&A deal volume fell ~22% quarter-over-quarter to a two-year low\n\n---\n\n### Notable Company Results\n\n| Company | Key Q4 Highlights |\n|---|---|\n| **SAP** | 30% cloud backlog growth to a record €77 billion |\n| **IBM** | Double-digit software and infrastructure growth; $12.5B generative AI pipeline |\n| **Ondas (ONDS)** | Record $30.1M revenue; 605% full-year growth |\n| **Target** | Declining traffic for four straight quarters; net income fell to $1.05B |\n\n---\n\n### Overall Takeaway\nQ4 2025 showed **mixed but generally resilient performance** across sectors, with strong results in tech and AI-driven businesses, while consumer-facing companies and small businesses faced headwinds from inflation and cautious spending.",
            },
