              "<table><tr><th>requirement_title</th><td>Lead and Scale 60+ Enterprise Sales Team</td></tr><tr><th>match_level</th><td>no_match</td></tr><tr><th>evidence</th><td>The capabilities document is a resume for John Doe, a graphic design graduate from the University of Minnesota whose objective is to &quot;Design apparel print for an innovative retail company.&quot; Work experience consists of entry-level retail roles (Sales Associate at American Eagle, Spa Consultant at Planet Beach, Sales Associate at Heartbreaker, Fashion Representative at Victoria&#x27;s Secret) and a brief brand ambassador volunteer role. The only leadership-adjacent experience cited is &quot;assisting in the training of coworkers&quot; at Victoria&#x27;s Secret. There is no evidence of enterprise sales experience, no experience managing sales teams, no multi-region leadership, and no track record of building or scaling teams of any size — let alone 60+ enterprise sales professionals.</td></tr><tr><th>gap_description</th><td>The candidate/company has no demonstrated enterprise sales experience, no sales management or leadership experience, no multi-region team-building track record, and no experience scaling teams. The background is in retail sales associate roles and graphic design, which are fundamentally different from leading a 60+ person enterprise B2B sales organization. Closing this gap would require hiring an entirely new senior sales leadership function and building enterprise sales infrastructure from scratch.</td></tr><tr><th>effort_to_close</th><td>high</td></tr></table>",
